  "articleBody": "Ever open a door and it just... sticks? Or maybe you notice a draft even when it's closed? Those are often signs that your door frame isn't quite right. It's super common for us to get questions about whether an existing frame can be salvaged or if a full replacement is needed. A lot of folks wonder if their door opening is still square and plumb, or if they can reuse the door, hinges, and latch they already have. Sometimes, the existing damage is pretty obvious, like rot or significant warping, but other times it's a subtle misalignment that causes all the trouble. If you're noticing these issues, it's worth taking a closer look. A professional can help you figure out what's going on, especially if the problems seem to be tied into the house framing itself. Don't just live with a sticky door; let's get it working smoothly again!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
